PRD: Investing Education + Paper Trading App
1. Product Overview
Product: A gamified investing education app for high school students ages 14–18.
Core idea: Students complete short investing lessons to unlock capabilities in a simulated brokerage account. They then use virtual money to practice investing in the stock market.
MVP goal: Demonstrate that a student can go from knowing nothing about investing to completing a lesson and using what they learned to make a simulated investment. Students should be able to “unlock” two of the features on the simulated brokerage account, while learning about the stock market. 

2. Core User Flow
The entire MVP should follow this flow:
Sign Up → Learn → Complete Quiz → Unlock Feature → Invest → Track Portfolio
Example:
Student creates an account
Student sees their virtual brokerage account
Trading features are initially locked
Student completes "What is a Stock?"
Student completes a short quiz
Limited stock trading becomes unlocked
Student receives $10,000 virtual cash
Student searches for a stock
Student is prompted to take a lesson before being able to buy a share of said stock
Student completes “Buying and Selling Stocks”
Student completes a short quiz
Student buys shares
Student sees the stock added to their portfolio
Student can track their simulated gains/losses

